course: dictionary
lesson: 6726
title: Oilbird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oilbird is a brown bird that flies at night. It lives in caves in South America and Trinidad, and it eats fruit. Its name is a clue to a sad old story, which you will read about below.
explain: «Some cave swiftlets of Asia and the oilbird of South America click to find their way in pitch-black caves, with clicks low enough for people to hear.» The clues are caves, pitch-black and click. Pitch-black means completely dark, so the oilbird must find its way in the dark by clicking.
explain: Clicking to find your way is called echolocation. The clicks bounce off walls and objects, and the bird listens to the echoes. A bat does the same thing, so the oilbird is a bit like a bat, but it is a bird.
fact: An oilbird is a brown bird that flies at night.
fact: Oilbirds live in caves in South America and Trinidad, and they eat fruit.
fact: Oilbirds find their way in the dark by clicking, which is called echolocation.
fact: The chicks get very fat, and long ago people boiled them to make oil for lamps and cooking. That is why the bird is called the oilbird.
exercise: «The oilbird flies in pitch-black caves.» What does pitch-black mean? | Full of water | Painted black | Bright and sunny | *Completely dark
exercise: Where do oilbirds live? | In trees in Australia | In rivers in Africa | *In caves in South America and Trinidad | In deserts and on ice
exercise: How does the oilbird find its way in the dark? | It sees by the light of the moon | It follows the stars | *By clicking, like a bat | It uses a torch
test: What does an oilbird eat? | *Fruit | Seeds from the ground | Insects | Fish
test: Why do people say the bird is called the oilbird? | *Because long ago people boiled the fat chicks to make oil | Because its feathers are oily to touch | Because it can make oil from its feathers | Because it lives near oil wells
exam: Using the clue «pitch-black caves», what does an oilbird most likely do to find its way? | Follows the light of the sun | *Clicks and listens to the echoes | Flies high above the trees to look for food | Waits by the cave door until morning
